MEMORY.md
.claude/

# Jekyll build output and local gem installs.
# Gemfile.lock stays untracked deliberately: the Actions workflow resolves
# dependencies itself (`bundler-cache: true`) under Ruby 3.2, and a lockfile
# generated locally under a different Ruby would pin platform-specific gems
# that the runner then has to re-resolve anyway.
_site/
.bundle/
.bundle-cache/
.jekyll-cache/
.jekyll-metadata
Gemfile.lock
